    "created_at": "2016-08-23T09:58:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-08-23T09:58:49Z",
    "body": "They can both start out as attributes in step 2, but yeah, _if_ they're attached to elements then _node1_ and _node2_ will be reassigned to those elements. So if _node1_ or _node2_ are attributes at step 6, then they're not attached. Saying \"node1 _or_ node2 are attributes\" would handle detached cases, then.\n\nStep 7 or 8 would still need some tweaking, I presume. Since you reverse engineered Gecko, I think that it all follows from \"If there is an owner element _add the attribute to the chain_ and walk up to the element\" (my emphasis).\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
